                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "Coin of the king of Armenia Khosrov I the Brave, 206-253. AE (Bronze, 23 mm, 5.99 g, 12 h). Bearded head of Khosrov I the Brave to left, wearing four-pointed tiara tied with a diadem; all within laurel wreath. Rev. 𐡌𐡋𐡁𐡏 / 𐡕𐡓𐡃𐡈 / ΛΙΛ ('Xsroe mlk' in Aramaic) in three lines within laurel wreath.\nThe inscriptions on these coins are often garbled and difficult to decipher, but they were likely minted under Khosrov I the Brave. He was the first Armenian king to issue coins since Tigranes VI in 66/7 AD—and, as it turned out, also the last (in Armenian line of Arsacid dynasty). He initially proved to be quite a successful ruler, but met his end in 253 when he was assassinated by Anak..",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
